@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+crew#661 CP1: HelmRelease tailscale/tailscale-operator has read UpgradeFailed since 2026-08-28T12:43Z, and guacamole waits behind it on a Flux dependency. Not the image name — idp#1030 fixed that, and diagnose run 33354635731 shows the registry-qualified image pulling clean ten times. The pod never starts because the values patch `runAsNonRoot: true` onto an image whose config declares no USER (registry config blob for docker.io/tailscale/k8s-operator:v1.102.3, read 2026-08-31): the kubelet refused the container 86 times in 28 minutes with "container has runAsNonRoot and image will run as root", and the 102 re-pulls of a container that never ran then burned Docker Hub's unauthenticated pull rate limit as a side effect. This PR removes the two flags the image cannot satisfy and excuses exactly those two rules at admission, scoped to this one pod — the same class and the same answer as the Lago images (commerce-exception.yaml).
+
+Optimised: 4 steps -> 2, 3 CI round trips -> 1; cut: the helm-retry break-glass hand (it retries into the same kubelet refusal) and a runAsUser-plus-HOME-volume postRenderer (disproven upstream by tailscale/tailscale#10638), leaving one values edit plus one scoped exception in a single wave
+
+Verify: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew661_a_nonroot_flag_on_a_root_image_never_starts.py`
+
+Breaker: n/a — this removes two manifest flags a root image cannot satisfy; nothing here retries or self-heals (Helm remediation keeps its existing bounded 3 retries)
+
+Control: platform/edge/tailscale-operator-exception.yaml
+
+Drill: chaos-pod-kill
+Tile: Ops → cluster-state; the tailscale and guacamole Kustomization rows go green when this lands
+
+## Options considered
+- Force a non-root uid (runAsUser 65532 plus a writable HOME via postRenderer): disproven upstream — the operator writes $HOME/.config at start and dies "permission denied on file creation" as any non-root uid (tailscale/tailscale#10638), and a volume-and-env wrapper to satisfy a policy is the stitching we do not ship. Rejected.
+- Dispatch the helm-retry break-glass hand: the release is not wedged on Helm, it is wedged on the kubelet refusing the container; a retry re-renders the same refused pod and spends the founder's attention on a mutation that cannot work. Rejected.
+- Chosen: upstream's own shipped posture (the chart sets no securityContext at all) plus a PolicyException scoped to the one pod, both rule spellings, precedent platform/edge/commerce-exception.yaml — measured from the image config, not assumed.
+
+## Architecture laws
+- LAW 1 zero-gravity: `platform/tailscale/operator.yaml`, `platform/edge/tailscale-operator-exception.yaml` -> the tailscale and guacamole rows on the estate state page
+- LAW 2 fractal: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew661_a_nonroot_flag_on_a_root_image_never_starts.py`
+- LAW 3 nervous system: `tests/test_incident_crew661_a_nonroot_flag_on_a_root_image_never_starts.py` (4: the two unsatisfiable flags stay out of the values; everything the image can satisfy still binds; the exception covers both rule spellings on every pod-making surface; the exception file is wired into the edge kustomization)
+- LAW 4 calibration: `platform/edge/tailscale-operator-exception.yaml` -> exactly 2 policies excused on 1 pod in 1 namespace; seccomp, no-privilege-escalation, drop-ALL, requests and limits all still bind
+Cost-delta-usd-month: 0
+
+## Definition of done
+1. Tracked item — crew#661 CP1
+2. Code or config — two flags out of the operator values; one scoped PolicyException
+3. Gate proved both ways — the cluster IS the failing side (86 kubelet refusals in run 33354635731); the passing side is this branch's kyverno rung rendering the excused pod clean
+4. Reference doc — the exception file's own header quotes the measurements and when it is reconsidered
+5. How-to and demo — merge; Flux reconciles tailscale within 1h (or one oke-check dispatch); HelmRelease goes Ready and guacamole follows
+6. Catalog entity — existing tailscale resource; crew#661 CP4 owns its Backstage section
+7. Operational proof — post-merge, the estate state page's tailscale row; the founder's next oke-check run shows HelmRelease Ready True
+8. Scheduled re-grade — the cluster-state receipt every 15 minutes; crew#661 CP2 adds the dedicated drill row
+9. Standard row — Networking; no provider name outside platform/
+10. Evidence block — below, attached by pr-evidence
+No-Issue: tracked on crew#661 (crew repo) CP1; the founder's word on crew#633 is "get it working"
+
+Author-session: a7b41022
+
+## Verification evidence
+```
+$ python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew661_a_nonroot_flag_on_a_root_image_never_starts.py
+....                                                                     [100%]
+4 passed in 10.11s
+```
+Kubelet refusal receipts: diagnose run 33354635731 (86x "container has runAsNonRoot and image will run as root"; 10 clean pulls of the registry-qualified image).
