@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+crew#722: enterprise-wide secrets rotation strategy. Founder 2026-08-31: "poorly designed enterprise-wide secrets rotation strategy, this will harm us badly if we let it slide." Twice in one week a vault write succeeded and the running program kept the old value (crew#506 CP4, crew#684); both were found by a person hitting a broken door. This wave ships the strategy (docs/policy/secrets-rotation.md, stages 1-5 with owners) and its two proving controls: a receipt row that goes red when any running pod is older than a Secret it consumes, and a daily canary drill that rotates a real vault entry and waits until the running pod answers with the new value. SLO 25 minutes, vault to pod, no hand.
+
+Optimised: 21 steps -> 9, 13 round trips -> 4; cut: the per-file build-test loop (13 files fixed one by one) became one scripted sweep + one batched write wave, and the second local suite run was cut because CI runs the 413-file suite once on this PR (R58).
+
+Verify: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew722_rotation_reaches_the_running_pod.py`
+Verify: `bin/idp-root-trust`
+
+## Options considered
+- kube-state-metrics + a PromQL rule: no metric relates a pod's start time to the write time of a Secret it references; building that join in PromQL means a recording rule per consumer — a list that rots. Rejected.
+- A new freshness exporter: a second instrument nobody reads (LAW 28) and a script for a problem the graded receipt already owns (LAW 43). Rejected.
+- Chosen: extend the estate's one graded instrument — the cluster-state receipt and its grader — plus a canary consumer on the estate's own reload standard, so the drill exercises exactly the road production secrets travel.
+
+## Architecture laws
+- LAW 1 zero-gravity: `platform/state/cluster-state.yaml`, `platform/state/rotation-canary.yaml`, `bin/idp-cluster-state`, `.github/workflows/oke-check.yml` (rotation-drill) -> the estate state row and the daily drill row
+- LAW 2 fractal: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew722_rotation_reaches_the_running_pod.py`
+- LAW 3 nervous system: `tests/test_incident_crew722_rotation_reaches_the_running_pod.py` (9: a stale-consumer receipt FAILS naming pod and Secret; a failed metadata list is -1 and FAILS, never a clean zero; a receipt predating the count FAILS; the collector flags the stale pod and honours grace, opt-out, Job pods and exempt namespaces; RBAC is list-only so a value read is not expressible; the canary mounts a file, reads once at start, carries probes and two spread replicas; the catalogue cron is the workflow's own cron; the drill never runs on a pull_request)
+- LAW 4 calibration: grace 900s after a write (an in-flight roll is not an incident); drill SLO 1500s = 600s ESO refresh + roll + 120s receipt loop + slack; drill max_age_hours 26 for a daily row
+Cost-delta-usd-month: 0 (one metadata list per 15-min collection; one 2x25m-CPU canary pod pair)
+Drill: rotation-canary
+Tile: the estate state page red rows (secret-freshness) and the drills table (rotation-canary) — both already on the founder's Backstage Ops view
+
+## Definition of done
+1. Tracked item — crew#722 CP2 + CP3
+2. Code or config — collector, grader, canary manifest, drill job, catalogue row, policy doc
+3. Gate proved both ways — proof obligation: the pre-fix state (a receipt whose pod predates a rotated Secret) FAILS the grader in test 4; the clean state passes in test 5
+4. Reference doc — docs/policy/secrets-rotation.md (the strategy, stage table, later waves CP4-CP6)
+5. How-to and demo — merge, then dispatch oke-check once: the rotation-drill job seeds the vault entry and the run log shows "ok rotation-canary the running pod answered with the rotated value after Ns"
+6. Catalog entity — existing idp component; the drill is a catalogue row, not a new entity
+7. Operational proof — the first scheduled rotation-drill run (17:06Z daily... cron "17 6 * * *", so 06:17Z) green; the estate state page shows the secret-freshness row
+8. Scheduled re-grade — the receipt every 15 minutes; the drill daily; drills/catalogue.yaml grades a missing run red within 26h
+9. Standard row — Secrets (rotation); no provider name outside platform/state
+10. Evidence block — below, attached by pr-evidence
+Standard: Secrets
+
+Author-session: a7b41022
