@@ -0,0 +1,56 @@
+crew#727: reconcile intervals are one estate value, and reconcile state is visible. Founder 2026-08-31, verbatim: "Set intervals consistently and deliberately across every HelmRelease and Kustomization. Not per-chart guesses. One value in the base patch — 10m for drift detection is a reasonable estate-wide default... Make the actual state visible instead of inferred." Measured spread before this wave: Kustomizations 34x1m + 14x10m + 1x1m0s, HelmReleases 24x1h + 2x10m — three spellings of a decision nobody made. The distinction the tooling now states: interval is drift detection only; time-to-land is the flux-system GitRepository poll (1m, untouched) plus the dependency chain — a new revision reconciles immediately whatever the drift value says.
+
+Optimised: 35 steps -> 7, 10 round trips -> 2; cut: wave 1 (74 interval lines) and wave 2 (timeouts, ESO refresh, retries, checkout pin — five knobs that would naively be five PRs) are two scripted passes riding ONE PR: one CI wave, one APPROVE. Raise-never-lower made wave 2 safe without per-chart review; pre-fix reds and the kustomize build proof ran locally (R58).
+
+Verify: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew727_intervals_are_one_estate_value.py`
+Verify: `python3 -c "import json; json.load(open('platform/estate-state/schema.json'))"`
+Verify: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew727_scattered_knobs_are_deliberate.py`
+
+## Options considered
+- Keep tuning intervals per chart: recreates the guessing — nobody could say why lago re-asserted hourly and traefik every minute; the founder's directive is exactly that this number is not per-chart knowledge. Rejected.
+- Set controller-level defaults via flux-system Deployment args: buries the value in gotk-components.yaml marked DO NOT EDIT, and the next flux bootstrap reverts it silently. Rejected.
+- Chosen: an explicit root kustomization.yaml in clusters/oke with one patch targeting every Flux Kustomization (flux-system's own included, overridden in-cluster), plus a test that pins the resources list to the directory so the explicit list can never silently drop-and-prune a file.
+
+## Architecture laws
+- LAW 1 zero-gravity: clusters/oke/kustomization.yaml -> the one patch every Kustomization interval comes from; platform/state/cluster-state.yaml + bin/idp-estate-state-build -> the reconcile table on the state page
+- LAW 2 fractal: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew727_intervals_are_one_estate_value.py`
+- LAW 3 nervous system: tests/test_incident_crew727_intervals_are_one_estate_value.py (5: every Kustomization/HelmRelease interval equals the one base-patch value; an unlisted file beside the root list is red before prune deletes its objects; the GitRepository poll stays at a minute so landing speed never regresses to the drift default; receipt rows carry the applied revision; the state page carries every reconcile row, not only the failed); tests/test_incident_crew727_scattered_knobs_are_deliberate.py (4: Flux timeouts are the 10m default or a pinned named exception with a reason; remediation retries are one value; every ExternalSecret refresh honours the 25m rotation SLO; one actions/checkout pin estate-wide)
+- LAW 4 calibration: `interval: 10m` in clusters/oke/kustomization.yaml -> drift re-assert (the founder's stated value); `interval: 1m0s` in clusters/oke/flux-system/gotk-sync.yaml -> time-to-land, untouched; HelmRepository 24h chart polling untouched (a different knob)
+Cost-delta-usd-month: 0 (fewer reconcile loops, not more: 34 Kustomizations drop from 1m to 10m re-assert)
+Drill: cluster-state
+Breaker: n/a — manifest-only interval normalisation plus one additive receipt field; no retry loop introduced
+Control: tests/test_incident_crew727_intervals_are_one_estate_value.py
+Tile: the estate state page (crew#648) gains the reconcile table — what is reconciling, when it last ran, ready or not, at which revision
+
+## Definition of done
+1. Tracked item — crew#727
+2. Code or config — root base patch, 74 interval lines in 26 manifests, collector revision field, builder reconcile table, schema row; wave 2: Flux timeouts to default-or-exception, 41 ExternalSecret refresh lines to 10m, retries, checkout pin
+3. Gate proved both ways — pre-fix run on the old tree: 3 failed (spread, revision, reconcile); post-fix: 5 passed (transcript below)
+4. Reference doc — the drift-vs-landing distinction is pinned in the test module docstring and the kustomization.yaml header, where CI holds it
+5. How-to and demo — merge; the next receipt populates the reconcile table on the estate state page; "did my merge land" is a read of the revision column
+6. Catalog entity — existing idp component; no new entity
+7. Operational proof — first post-merge receipt shows the reconcile table populated and every Kustomization at 10m
+8. Scheduled re-grade — the receipt every 15 minutes; the interval test pins the one value on every CI run
+9. Standard row — GitOps (Flux); no provider name introduced
+10. Evidence block — below, attached by pr-evidence
+
+## Verification evidence
+```
+$ python3 -m pytest -q -o addopts= tests/test_incident_crew727_intervals_are_one_estate_value.py   # pre-fix tree
+3 failed, 2 passed   (failed: one-estate-value spread, receipt revision, state-page reconcile)
+$ python3 scratchpad/crew727_wave.py
+normalized 74 interval lines in 32 files
+$ python3 -m pytest -q -o addopts= tests/test_incident_crew727_intervals_are_one_estate_value.py
+5 passed
+kustomize build proof: raw objects=93 built=93 missing=[] extra=[]; built Kustomization intervals {'10m': 49} (flux-system's own included)
+$ python3 -m pytest -q -o addopts= tests/test_incident_crew727_scattered_knobs_are_deliberate.py   # wave 2, mid-pass
+1 failed, 3 passed   (failed: hindsight install.retries=5 — flow-style line the sweep missed; fixed)
+$ python3 -m pytest -q -o addopts= tests/test_incident_crew727_scattered_knobs_are_deliberate.py tests/test_incident_crew727_intervals_are_one_estate_value.py
+9 passed
+```
+
