+crew#722 (founder 2026-08-31, comment 5472793578): "a rigorous lifecycle document with a diagram, strongly audited and monitored at every stage." One page: a six-stage diagram (Mint -> Distribute -> Consume -> Rotate -> Prove -> Revoke) and a per-stage table naming the receipt that proves each stage and the alarm that screams when it fails. Stages 1-5 are LIVE and name the exact control (including the receipt row and canary drill merged in idp#1029); stage 6 (revoke) is named PLANNED CP6 — the gap is on the page, not hidden.
+
+Optimised: 5 steps -> 2, 3 round trips -> 1; cut: a separate diagram asset and a per-stage doc set — one Markdown file carries the mermaid diagram and the six-stage table, and one push wave carries branch, commit, PR and board note.
+
+## Options considered
+- Six per-stage runbooks under docs/runbooks/: six pages nobody reads end to end, and the stage-to-stage handoff (the exact place both incidents lived) falls between pages. Rejected.
+- A diagram image checked in beside the text: an asset that rots the first time a stage changes; mermaid in the Markdown is regenerated by the renderer on every read. Rejected.
+- Chosen: one docs/policy page, diagram plus table, every row naming a control that already exists in git or a PLANNED wave tracked on crew#722.
+
+## Architecture laws
+- LAW 1 zero-gravity: `docs/policy/secrets-lifecycle.md` -> the one page a buyer's engineer reads before the vault
+- LAW 2 fractal: `n/a: docs-only — no code changed; the controls the page names are each proved by their own merged tests (idp#1029)`
+- LAW 3 nervous system: `n/a: docs-only — the alarms column names the live graders (cluster-state receipt, rotation-canary drill), which fail red on their own schedules`
+- LAW 4 calibration: 900s consume grace, 1500s drill SLO, 26h drill max age — the page quotes the merged values, it does not invent new ones
+Cost-delta-usd-month: 0 (a Markdown page)
+Drill: rotation-canary
+Tile: Backstage TechDocs for the idp component — the page renders under docs/policy
+
+## Definition of done
+1. Tracked item — crew#722 comment 5472793578 (the founder's lifecycle-doc request)
+2. Code or config — docs/policy/secrets-lifecycle.md only
+3. Gate proved both ways — n/a: docs-only; the named controls carry their own both-ways tests, merged in idp#1029
+4. Reference doc — this page is the reference doc; it links the strategy page shipped in idp#1029
+5. How-to and demo — open the page: the diagram is the demo, the table is the how-to per stage
+6. Catalog entity — existing idp component; renders in its TechDocs
+7. Operational proof — stages 1-5 rows each name a control already running (receipt each 15 min, drill daily)
+8. Scheduled re-grade — the named graders re-run on their own schedules; the page holds no numbers a clock can rot
+9. Standard row — Secrets; no provider name outside platform rows, none added here
+10. Evidence block — the merged idp#1029 checks page and this PR's own green run
+Standard: Secrets
