@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+crew#722: the first scheduled canary seed died on the runner with OCI "keyId cannot be an empty string" (oke-check run 33353772359, rotation-drill). bin/idp-cloud resolved a brand-new secret's vault and key only from `tofu output`; the runner has no tofu, so an empty string went straight to the create_secret call, rotation-canary was never seeded, and backstage/rotation-canary ExternalSecret is red on the estate state page. This PR makes the resolution tofu-free where it can be and loud where it cannot: env override first, then the metadata every ACTIVE sibling secret in the compartment already carries (the majority vault wins, so one stray secret cannot steer the key), then tofu state where a machine has it, then BLIND exit 2 -- an empty id never reaches the API again.
+
+Optimised: 6 steps -> 3, 2 CI round trips -> 1; cut: installing tofu plus a state backend read on the drill job (credentials a drill never needed) -- the sibling secrets' own metadata already names the vault and key.
+
+Verify: `python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew722_seed_needs_no_tofu.py`
+
+## Options considered
+- Install opentofu on the rotation-drill job and init the state backend: adds state-backend credentials to a job that only writes one canary secret, and every other tofu-less caller of idp-cloud stays broken. Rejected.
+- Hardcode the estate vault and key OCIDs as workflow vars: LAW 46 (a file never names where the machine lives) and it rots on the next vault rebuild. Rejected.
+- Chosen: resolve from the compartment's own ACTIVE secrets -- no new credentials, no state read, correct on every machine oci works on, and a BLIND that keeps the drill red when nothing can be resolved.
+
+## Architecture laws
+- LAW 1 zero-gravity: `bin/idp-cloud` -> the one road every estate vault write and the daily rotation-canary drill take
+- LAW 2 fractal: `bash -n bin/idp-cloud && python3 -m pytest -q tests/test_incident_crew722_seed_needs_no_tofu.py`
+- LAW 3 nervous system: `tests/test_incident_crew722_seed_needs_no_tofu.py` (3: siblings' metadata creates with the majority vault's key when tofu is absent; an empty compartment with no tofu exits BLIND and never puts an empty id on the wire; the env override is used untouched)
+- LAW 4 calibration: majority-vault selection tolerates one stray secret in a second vault; BLIND exit 2 keeps the drill row red rather than silently green
+Cost-delta-usd-month: 0 (one already-made list call re-read; no new jobs)
+Drill: rotation-canary
+Tile: the estate state page -- backstage/rotation-canary ExternalSecret goes green once the next dispatched oke-check seeds the entry
+
+## Definition of done
+1. Tracked item -- crew#722 CP3 follow-through (seed run 33353772359 red)
+2. Code or config -- resolve_vault_and_key in bin/idp-cloud, used by both former tofu call sites
+3. Gate proved both ways -- pre-fix: run 33353772359 rotation-drill red on the empty keyId; post-fix: the three tests pass with tofu absent from PATH
+4. Reference doc -- docs/policy/secrets-rotation.md stage 1 (Mint) unchanged; this is its transport made runner-safe
+5. How-to and demo -- merge, dispatch oke-check once: rotation-drill seeds rotation-canary and the run log shows "ok rotation-canary the running pod answered with the rotated value after Ns"
+6. Catalog entity -- existing idp component
+7. Operational proof -- the next rotation-drill run green; the rotation-canary ExternalSecret row leaves the estate state red list
+8. Scheduled re-grade -- the drill daily (06:17Z); drills/catalogue.yaml grades a missing run red within 26h
+9. Standard row -- Secrets (rotation); no provider OCID added to any file
+10. Evidence block -- the incident run log and this PR's green checks
+Standard: Secrets
+
+No-Issue: tracked on crew#722 comment 5472793578 -- the crew issue stays open for waves CP4-CP6, so this closes nothing in idp
+
+Author-session: a7b41022
